# Security-relevant surface. A change here alters what the gate can see or
# who must review it:
#   .githooks/**        pattern lists and the hooks that run the gate
#   bin/gate_scan.py    the gate itself
#   .github/**          the CI that runs the gate
#   CODEOWNERS          this file: who reviews the lines above
# Review these as security changes, not docs changes. The CI surface pin
# (bin/gate_surface_pin.sh) blocks the same paths, so they land only by an
# admin merge after review.
#
# The gate's tests and fixtures get the same reviewer, but are not pinned:
# they never run in the gate job, so editing them cannot change what the
# gate sees. They are where a gate change is exercised, so read them with it.
/.githooks/             @wildbuffaloman
/bin/                   @wildbuffaloman
/.github/               @wildbuffaloman
/CODEOWNERS             @wildbuffaloman
/docs/CODEOWNERS        @wildbuffaloman
/tests/test_gate*.py    @wildbuffaloman
/tests/fixtures/        @wildbuffaloman
